    const Section(
      title: 'History & Systems Review:',
      content: 'Key areas to assess:\n- **Pain characterization**: Burning, throbbing quality. Spontaneous pain without provocation. Allodynia (pain from normally non-painful stimuli — clothing, light touch, air movement). Hyperalgesia (exaggerated pain response to mildly painful stimuli). Pain distribution — does it follow a dermatomal pattern (it should NOT in CRPS — it is regional and non-dermatomal).\n- **Vasomotor changes**: Color changes (red, blue, mottled, pale) — ask if they fluctuate. Temperature asymmetry — does the hand feel warmer or cooler than the other side? Can change over time (warm early, cool later).\n- **Sudomotor changes**: Sweating asymmetry — increased or decreased sweating compared to the unaffected hand.\n- **Edema**: Onset, distribution, does it fluctuate. Non-pitting edema is common in CRPS.\n- **Motor/trophic changes**: Weakness (not from a specific nerve or root lesion), reduced ROM, tremor, dystonia. Trophic changes: altered hair growth, nail changes (brittle, ridged, discolored), skin changes (shiny, thin, or thickened).\n- **Timeline**: Symptoms should follow a precipitating event (fracture in this case) and be disproportionate to the inciting event. The 3-month timeline is typical for CRPS presentation.\n- **Psychological screening**: CRPS does NOT equal malingering or somatization — but comorbid anxiety, depression, and PTSD are common and affect outcomes. Screen with PHQ-9 and GAD-7. Assess pain catastrophizing (PCS).\n- **Functional impact**: Dominant hand involvement in a teacher — cannot write, type, carry materials, or manage a classroom. Impact on ADLs: dressing, hygiene, cooking, driving.\n- **Prior treatments**: Has she received any treatment for CRPS specifically, or has it been managed as persistent fracture pain? Many CRPS cases are delayed in diagnosis because the condition is not recognized.\n- **Workers\' compensation status**: Work injury? Claim status? IME scheduled? Adversarial interactions with insurance?',
